@startuml
'https://plantuml.com/sequence-diagram

'see https://ashend.medium.com/openid-connect-backchannel-logout-144a3198d2a
'for a quick description of back-channel logout.

actor UserAgent
participant Schoolbox
participant Paperly

activate UserAgent
activate Paperly

note left of UserAgent
  The user agent has a valid Schoolbox and Paperly session.

  The standard back-channel logout process is for the
  oAuth provider (Schoolbox) to track its relying parties
  (in this case Paperly), and send a back-channel logout
  request to each one.
end note

UserAgent -> Schoolbox : sends logout request
Schoolbox -> Schoolbox : checks if a Paperly session exists
Schoolbox -> Paperly : sends logout token
Paperly -> Paperly : verifies logout token
Paperly -> Paperly : destroys session
deactivate Paperly

Paperly -> Schoolbox : responds with status of logout request

deactivate UserAgent

Schoolbox -> UserAgent : displays login page

@enduml
